## Blueprint Templates — Condensed Guide

**Goal:** Declarative UI in `.blp`; logic in TypeScript. Prefer bindings; avoid hardcoded state.

### Core principles

- Use Blueprint for GTK UI; follow GNOME HIG.
- Keep UIs declarative; avoid constructing widgets in code.
- Add namespaces first: `using Gtk 4.0; using Adw 1;`.
- Template names start with `$`; extend correct base class (e.g. `Adw.Window`, `Adw.Bin`).
- Expose only needed children via `InternalChildren`.

### Template skeleton

```blp
using Gtk 4.0; using Adw 1;

template $MyWidget : Gtk.Box {
  Label title { label: bind template.title; hexpand: true; xalign: 0; }
}
```

### Binding (default)

- `bind template.prop` for display; `bind template.prop bidirectional` for editable inputs.
- Use expressions for simple transforms; avoid callbacks for presentation.
- Prefer bind over magic constants; compute `visible`, `sensitive`, `label` in-place.

```blp
Label err { label: bind template.error; visible: bind template.has_error as <bool>; styles: ["error"]; }
Entry edit { text: bind template.title bidirectional; }
```

### Signals in `.blp`, logic in TS

- Connect in `.blp` (e.g. `clicked => $_onSave();`).
- Implement in class; annotate with `@Gtk.Template.Callback()` when appropriate.
- Use consistent `_onXxx` naming.

```blp
Button save { action-name: "app.save"; clicked => $_onSave(); }
```

```ts
@Gtk.Template.Callback()
_on_save() { this.emit("save-requested"); }
```

### Minimal TypeScript registration

```ts
import GObject from "@girs/gobject-2.0";
import Gtk from "@girs/gtk-4.0";
import Template from "./my-widget.blp";

export class MyWidget extends Gtk.Box {
  static {
    GObject.registerClass(
      {
        GTypeName: "MyWidget",
        Template,
        InternalChildren: ["title", "save"],
        Properties: {
          title: GObject.ParamSpec.string(
            "title",
            "Title",
            "",
            GObject.ParamFlags.READWRITE,
            ""
          ),
        },
      },
      this
    );
  }
  declare _title: Gtk.Label;
  declare _save: Gtk.Button;
}
```

### Actions, menus, and state

- Prefer `GAction`/`action-name` over manual `clicked` where possible.
- Bind `action-target` to template state.
- Use `MenuButton.menu-model` for menus; do not build menus in code when declarative works.

```blp
Button { action-name: "app.export"; action-target: bind template.doc_id; }
MenuButton { icon-name: "open-menu-symbolic"; menu-model: template.menu; }
```

### Conditional UI

- Toggle visibility/sensitivity with boolean binds; compute labels inline.

```blp
Button submit {
  sensitive: bind template.form_valid;
  label: bind template.loading ? "Loading…" : "Submit";
}
```

### Layout defaults

- Prefer shallow hierarchies; use spacing/margins over nested boxes.
- Use `hexpand/halign/valign` intentionally for responsiveness.

```blp
Box root {
  orientation: vertical; spacing: 12;
  margin-top: 24; margin-bottom: 24; margin-start: 24; margin-end: 24;
  Box header {
    orientation: horizontal; spacing: 6;
    Label title { label: bind template.title; hexpand: true; xalign: 0; styles: ["title-1"]; }
    Button close { icon-name: "window-close-symbolic"; clicked => $_on_close(); }
  }
}
```

### Accessibility essentials

- Provide meaningful labels/`accessible-name` for interactives.
- Preserve keyboard navigation; avoid focus traps.
- Use tooltips only for non-obvious controls.

### Checklist

- ✅ Bindings > hardcoded values; actions > ad‑hoc handlers.
- ✅ Split complex UIs into multiple templates; meaningful names.
- ✅ Only expose `InternalChildren` you must access in code.
- ✅ Keep margins/spacing consistent; prefer Adwaita styles.
- ❌ No business logic in `.blp`; avoid deep container nesting.
- ❌ Don’t connect signals in code when `.blp` can do it.
